@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About / Help</PageTitle>

<h3>About this Blazor App</h3>

<p>
    This sample demonstrates how Blazor supports visual and event-driven programming through reusable components, data binding using @@bind-like syntax, event handlers like @@onclick, and routing using the @@page directive.
</p>

<h4>Key Concepts</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Components: Reusable UI pieces. This app uses TaskCard and AppointmentCard components.</li>
    <li>Routing: Pages use the @@page directive to map URLs to components.</li>
    <li>Data Binding: Forms use @@bind to synchronize UI with model properties.</li>
    <li>Events: Buttons and inputs trigger C# methods with @@onclick and form submission events.</li>
    <li>Conditional Rendering: Components show or hide pieces of UI using C# logic inside Razor.</li>
    <li>Parameters: Parent pages pass data into child components via component parameters.</li>
</ul>
